    "created_at": "2021-04-15T16:51:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-04-15T16:51:52Z",
    "body": "Starship is just a prompt--we don't do any execution of commands ourselves aside from what we need to draw the prompt. In fact, we *use* `PROMPT_COMMAND` (and its analogous commands in other shells) to make starship work. Without some feature like this, it simply wouldn't be possible to make an external command like starship work.\r\n\r\nIf you want to use PROMPT_COMMAND yourself, you can hook an existing command into starship using `starship_precmd_user_func`. See [here](https://starship.rs/advanced-config/#custom-pre-prompt-and-pre-execution-commands-in-bash) for details.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
