    "updated_at": "2021-04-17T06:16:06Z",
    "body": "Unfortunately, I'm not a powershell user so I'm not really sure.\r\n\r\nThe reason we have that feature for bash is because the bash pre-prompt execution story is a mess (only one function, can be knocked out accidentally by other functions). We offer that as a convenience for bash so that you don't wind up having to dig through a mess of weird invocations to add your own functionality. For ZSH/fish, it's pretty easy to add yourself.\r\n\r\nIf it turns out there's a need for this in other shells, we could add that feature to those as well? Though it's unclear to me exactly how to support that, given that we have so many other shells now.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
